  "upstream": [
    "CVE-2026-97042"
  ],
  "summary": "Building a malicious package that uses \"//go:cgo_import_dynamic\" or links against a crafted PE object on Windows could…",
  "details": "Building a malicious package that uses \"//go:cgo_import_dynamic\" or links against a crafted PE object on Windows could pass unsafe library arguments to the external linker. The compiler only checked the first character of the library name in \"//go:cgo_import_dynamic\" directives and skipped validation in cgo-generated files. In addition, on Windows, \"cmd/cgo\" and \"cmd/link\" did not validate imported DLL names extracted from PE object files before emitting \"-l<name>\" flags for the external linker, allowing a crafted DLL name containing \"..\" path traversal or special characters to reference arbitrary files on disk. The compiler now validates every character of the library name in \"//go:cgo_import_dynamic\" directives (including in cgo-generated files on Windows) and rejects \"..\" path traversal, and \"cmd/cgo\" and \"cmd/link\" reject PE imported DLL names containing path separators, \"..\", \":\", or leading \"-\" or \"@\".",
  "severity": [
    {
      "type": "CVSS_V3",
      "score": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H"
    }
  ],
